@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@accessToken = replace-with-a-bearer-token
@currentUserId = replace-with-current-user-id
@otherUserId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@conversationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@clientMessageId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@messageId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004
@readyOwnedMediaObjectId = replace-with-a-Ready-Message-scoped-media-id-you-own
@notOwnedMediaObjectId = replace-with-a-media-id-you-do-not-own-or-that-is-not-Ready

### Unauthenticated failure: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations

### List caller-owned conversations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get or create a conversation (201; repeated calls reuse the same id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{otherUserId}}"
}

### Self conversation failure: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{currentUserId}}"
}

### Unknown participant: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
}

### Thread page, newest first, with optional in-thread search
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?q=hello
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Older thread page using the response's nextCursor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?cursor=replace-with-nextCursor
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Invalid cursor failure: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?cursor=not-a-cursor
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Non-participant failure: 404 (the route does not confirm the conversation exists)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Send over HTTP; retry the same clientMessageId for an idempotent 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "{{clientMessageId}}",
  "body": "Hello from CompanyHQ"
}

### Send with an attachment: upload multipart bytes to POST /api/media?scope=Message first.
### The response is already Ready, Scope Message, and owned by this caller; there is no /complete route.
### 201; the response's mediaObjectId echoes back and the attachment is read via
### GET {{baseUrl}}/api/media/{{readyOwnedMediaObjectId}}, gated by MessagePolicy, not this route.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "{{messageId}}",
  "body": "Photo attached",
  "mediaObjectId": "{{readyOwnedMediaObjectId}}"
}

### Rejected attachment failure: 400 (media not owned by the caller, wrong scope, or not Ready)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "{{messageId}}",
  "body": "This attachment reference is rejected",
  "mediaObjectId": "{{notOwnedMediaObjectId}}"
}

### Blocked-send contract: still 201; response has no suppressed field and no delivery occurs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "{{messageId}}",
  "body": "This is accepted silently when the recipient has blocked the sender."
}

### Flagged sender to an ordinary account: still 201; message is stored for the sender only
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientMessageId": "{{messageId}}",
  "body": "A message from a flagged account is accepted silently."
}

### Flagged sender to the Admin account: 201 and delivered (operator carve-out)
### Messages sent to a flagged recipient are also delivered; neither case has a special wire shape.

### Mark read (204; participant only, otherwise 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Mute and unmute (204; mute changes notifications, not delivery)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/mute
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/unmute
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Clear this side only (204; rows remain in Postgres)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/clear
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Close for both participants (204); subsequent reads show IsClosed and sends fail with 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/{{conversationId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Unread badge total
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Operator-only route: open/reuse an Admin participant thread
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/with/{{otherUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Operator route failure for a non-admin: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conversations/with/{{otherUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer replace-with-client-token

### Receive-only SignalR hub: connect with the JWT as ?access_token=...
### wss://host/hubs/messages?access_token={{accessToken}}
### Events: MessageReceived(ClientMessageDto), ConversationRead(conversationId, readAt).
### The hub has no send method; refetch after reconnect.
